  "summary": "The study fabricated additive-free Ti3C2Tx electrodes from MILD-derived MXene using one aqueous ink for extrusion printing and four solvent-transferred organic inks (NMP, DMSO, DMF, and ethanol) for inkjet printing. These are distinct printed-electrode formulations; print-pass number, device connections, and line gap were not counted as separate electrodes. The NMP inkjet-printed MSC was the headline/best performer, reaching 562 F cm\u22123 at <N>=25 and 12 mF cm\u22122. The aqueous extrusion-printed MSC reached 43 mF cm\u22122 at <N>=5; individual capacitance metrics were not reported for the DMSO, DMF, or ethanol MSCs. Mass loading, BET surface area, pore metrics, tortuosity, and electrode-specific d-spacing were not reported."
}